    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but if they're just holding the money, what happens if the seller tries to back out or if they don't fix something they promised? how does the escrow person decide who gets the cash?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The escrow agent doesn't decide who gets the cash; they act strictly according to the terms laid out in the purchase agreement. If the seller breaches the contract—like failing to make agreed-upon repairs—the buyer can instruct the escrow agent to release funds to them or potentially terminate the contract. If the buyer backs out without fault, the earnest money might be claimed by the seller based on the contract terms.",
