      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it requires trust, the escrow agent operates under strict legal obligations and is not making subjective judgments. In case of a major dispute where the terms are unclear, the escrow agent's primary role is to pause the transaction and refer the matter to legal counsel or the contractually designated parties. This usually involves legal review to determine the proper next steps before any funds are released.",
